-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ה/5 (10.10.2024): הסכם קיבוצי עם ארגון המורים העל יסודיים מיום 23.09.2024
-- The main points of the collective agreement of 23.9.2024 between the
-- local-government employers and the secondary teachers' organization for
-- the upper divisions: a one-time grant for תשפ"ד, the Oz 2023 shekel
-- supplement in four pulses, the 38-hour work week, role rewards, the
-- school role reward, principals' supplements, the supplement for
-- employees outside the reform, special contracts, the retirement grant,
-- and the return of the strike days of September 2024.
--
-- The agreement's rules are encoded in its own file
-- (l4/agreements/oz-latmura/2024-09-23_oz-latmura_work-week-restructuring.l4),
-- which this circular imports: a circular applies the agreement and does
-- not re-encode it (MMS-521, MMS-663). Each row of §§1–39 the agreement
-- prints is cited "as in the agreement of 23.9.2024", by the rule that
-- encodes it there (this §38 is the agreement's §43, this §39 its §44);
-- what the circular says of its own — §14(טז)'s order of publishing, §30(ג)'s
-- second example, §§40–44 — is encoded here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `2024-09-23_oz-latmura_work-week-restructuring`
IMPORT minimum_wage_law
IMPORT annual_leave_law
IMPORT womens_work_law

-- Time in the regulative rules is counted in school months of תשפ"ה
-- (common.l4: September 2024 = 1, October 2024 = 2, November 2024 = 3,
-- January 2025 = 5, April 2025 = 8), unless a rule says otherwise.

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: §8 lowers the Oz
-- agreement's position base from 40 weekly hours to 38 and allows up to 12
-- beyond it, and leaves §9's working windows as they were: an hour of the
-- position is a weekly hour and a lesson, not 60 minutes of presence
-- (convention position.hour-beyond-unit), and the week the law counts is the
-- clock's, which §9's windows bound and the Oz agreement's §§9 and 14 weigh
-- against §3 (MMS-676). The retirement grant left out of the hour value for
-- overtime is paid once, for no hour worked.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: the words the search found are
-- not on its subject: ‘בעל’ is holding or having (‘בעל תואר’, ‘בעל רישיון’,
-- ‘בעל הסמכה’), not a husband; ‘בעל-פה’ is ‘orally’; none gives pay or
-- other remuneration by sex.

§ `תשפ"ה/5 הסכם קיבוצי 23.09.2024`

-- not weighed against `the Equal Opportunities Law`: §8(ג) puts annex ב'
-- in place of the Oz agreement's annex א', the mother teachers' week; the
-- mother teacher is the one the earlier agreements define (the Oz
-- agreement's §11(ג) keeps their definition), the mother teacher of the takanon's §1.13.1 (and of
-- the base agreement's §7(ג) in the reform), and the fathers it leaves out
-- of §4(א) are weighed there, on the card mother-position-fathers
-- (F-1.13-e, F-ofek-hadash-base-7-c).

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 The letterhead, date (10.10.2024), reference number, circular number, addressee (the owners of the upper divisions), greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 Background: the agreement was signed on 23.9.2024 between the local-government centre, the three large cities and the regional centre and the secondary teachers' organization, and approved by the Treasury's wages commissioner; the circular sets out its main points.

-- not weighed against `the Severance Pay Law`: §§7(ד), 14, 20 and 24(ד)
-- counts the Oz 2023 shekel supplement, the school role allowance, the
-- principal's and deputy's supplements and the 2023 shekel supplement in
-- the wage severance is computed on, and §§5(ח) and 37(ו) leaves the grant
-- and the retirement grant out of it. Which components count, §13 sends to
-- the regulations, which compute that wage by the collective agreement that
-- applies (as the takanon's §1.28.2.3 brings them): a component counted
-- adds to the severance, and for one left out the agreement's word is what
-- the law looks to; §13ב's minimum-wage floor holds whatever is counted.

-- not weighed against `the Sick Pay Law`: 37(ו) keeps the retirement grant
-- out of the compensation for unused sick days; the law gives sick pay for
-- an absence and redeems no day left unused at the end of the service, so
-- what that compensation counts is no right the law puts a floor under.

§§ `1–39, כפי שההסכם מיום 23.9.2024 קובע אותם`

